From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lukasz M <lukasz1992m+openwrt@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi mt76 npu set up napi before the rx interrupt

mt76_npu_rx_queue_init() requested the NPU rx interrupt and only then
added the NAPI the handler schedules.  The NPU keeps running across a
driver reload, so its interrupt can be pending when the irq is requested:
the handler then schedules a NAPI with no poll function and the kernel
jumps to 0 in net_rx_action (seen on an AN7552 reloading mt7915e).

Add, fill and enable the NAPI first, and take it down again if the
interrupt cannot be had.

Signed-off-by: Lukasz M <lukasz1992m+openwrt@gmail.com>
---
--- a/npu.c
+++ b/npu.c
@@ -285,14 +285,22 @@ int mt76_npu_rx_queue_init(struct mt76_d
 		goto out;
 	}
 
-	err = devm_request_irq(dev->dev, irq, mt76_npu_irq_handler,
-			       IRQF_SHARED, name, q);
-	if (err)
-		goto out;
-
+	/*
+	 * NAPI first: the NPU keeps running across a driver reload and its
+	 * interrupt can be pending already, and the handler schedules
+	 * dev->napi[qid] straight away.
+	 */
 	netif_napi_add(dev->napi_dev, &dev->napi[qid], mt76_npu_rx_poll);
 	mt76_npu_fill_rx_queue(dev, q);
 	napi_enable(&dev->napi[qid]);
+
+	err = devm_request_irq(dev->dev, irq, mt76_npu_irq_handler,
+			       IRQF_SHARED, name, q);
+	if (err) {
+		napi_disable(&dev->napi[qid]);
+		netif_napi_del(&dev->napi[qid]);
+		mt76_npu_queue_cleanup(dev, q);
+	}
 out:
 	mutex_unlock(&dev->mutex);
 
